# 4. Three-case state machine — bench/references.md §4, written with a
#    variant and a match (2026-08-29; it was a chain of equality tests on
#    numeric codes until this phase, because Phase 1 had no sum types):
#
#   λs:?. match s { Idle _ -> `Running {} | Running _ -> `Stopped {}
#                 | Stopped _ -> `Idle {} }
#
# `C-n` in a match is AddArm, which is the only way a constructor comes
# into being, and it lands in the constructor slot so the case can be
# named on the spot. The three names are the only content here: everything
# else is one keystroke per node.

\
s
.
s
|          # match s {} — the scrutinee is `?`, so it opens with no arms

# three cases, named where they are minted
C-n
